			<heading>
				Deliver Me from My Enemies
			</heading>
			<heading>
				To the choirmaster: according to Do Not Destroy. A Miktam(1) of David, when Saul sent men to watch his house in order to kill him.
			</heading>
			<begin-paragraph>
			</begin-paragraph>
			<v n="1">rise up against me;</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19059002">
			</marker>
			<v n="2">bloodthirsty men.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19059003">
			</marker>
			<v n="3">For no transgression or sin of mine, O Lord ,</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19059004">
			</marker>
			<v n="4">Awake, come to meet me, and see!</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19059005">
			</marker>
			<v n="5">spare none of those who treacherously plot evil. Selah</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19059006">
			</marker>
			<v n="6">and prowling about the city.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19059007">
			</marker>
			<v n="7">“Who,” they think, “will hear us?”</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19059008">
			</marker>
			<v n="8">you hold all the nations in derision.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19059009">
			</marker>
			<v n="9">my fortress.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19059010">
			</marker>
			<v n="10">look in triumph on my enemies.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19059011">
			</marker>
			<v n="11">shield!</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19059012">
			</marker>
			<v n="12">For the cursing and lies that they utter,</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19059013">
			</marker>
			<v n="13">the ends of the earth. Selah</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19059014">
			</marker>
			<v n="14">and prowling about the city.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19059015">
			</marker>
			<v n="15">and growl if they do not get their fill.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19059016">
			</marker>
			<v n="16">the day of my distress.</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v19059017">
			</marker>
